{"id": "55", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "raw_output": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "gt": "You can prevent birds from building nests on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch and the top of the porch if it has open rafters. This will block the birds from reaching spaces they often choose to build their nests. If you have a light fixture, you can also install bird netting over it, but make sure the netting is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs and doesn't entangle birds. Another method is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch, as this can scare birds away. Remember to move the plastic hawk periodically to prevent the birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 21.796, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.82, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "57", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "raw_output": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "gt": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves and top of your porch with staples. Additionally, you can install bird netting over your light fixture to deter birds from accessing it. Another option is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away. It's important to note that any product used to deter birds should be nonflammable and safe to use.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 21.589, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.48, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "58", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "raw_output": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This will prevent birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests, which can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease. (Passage 1:4)\n2. Install bird netting over the top of your light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs, and make sure it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. (Passage 2:1)\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch. Move the plastic hawk periodically to keep the birds from becoming accustomed to its presence. (Passage 3:1)\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, you can keep birds from building nests on your porch by using bird netting, installing bird netting over your light fixture, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 21.733, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.39, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "59", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "raw_output": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun (Passage 1:4). This will prevent birds from reaching the areas they often choose to build their nests.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it (Passage 2:1). Choose a non-flammable netting that is safe to use around light bulbs, and ensure that it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds from the area (Passage 3:1). Move the plastic hawk periodically to avoid the birds becoming accustomed to it.\n\nPlease note that the effectiveness of these methods may vary depending on the type of birds and the location of your porch. If the above methods do not work, you may need to consider other solutions or consult with a professional for assistance.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 21.662, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.87, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "60", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "raw_output": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a staple gun. This prevents birds from accessing the spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but remember to move it periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building a nest on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to keep birds from building a nest on your porch is:\n\nAttach bird netting to the eaves or install bird netting over the light fixture, and/or mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 21.742, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "62", "pred": "This will make the selected browser the default for opening hyperlinks and web content in Windows.", "raw_output": "To set the default browser in Windows, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and selecting the Settings icon, or by pressing the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. Click on the \"System\" option (which includes display, notifications, apps, and power settings).\n3. In the left pane, select \"Default apps.\"\n4. On the right side, scroll down to the \"Web browser\" section.\n5. Click on the current default browser (e.g., Microsoft Edge) to open the \"Choose an app\" menu.\n6. Select the browser you want to set as default (e.g., Google Chrome or Mozilla Firefox).\n\nThis will make the selected browser the default for opening hyperlinks and web content in Windows.", "gt": "Method 1 of 2 in passage 2 provides the steps to set the default web browser in Windows 7.", "question": "set default browser to windows", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 26.08, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.78, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "63", "pred": "This will make the selected browser the default for opening hyperlinks and web content in Windows.", "raw_output": "To set the default browser in Windows, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and selecting the Settings icon, or by pressing the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. Click on the \"System\" option (which includes display, notifications, apps, and power settings).\n3. In the left pane, select \"Default apps.\"\n4. On the right side, scroll down to the \"Web browser\" section.\n5. Click on the current default browser (e.g., Microsoft Edge) to open the \"Choose an app\" menu.\n6. Select the browser you want to set as default (e.g., Google Chrome or Mozilla Firefox).\n\nThis will make the selected browser the default for opening hyperlinks and web content in Windows.", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": "set default browser to windows", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 26.044, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.88, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "64", "pred": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to either have it collected after removing the blue field (which is then burned peacefully and the ashes buried) or to burn the flag yourself in a proper ceremony. During the ceremony, the flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "raw_output": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to either have it collected after removing the blue field (which is then burned peacefully and the ashes buried) or to burn the flag yourself in a proper ceremony. During the ceremony, the flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "gt": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is either by separating the blue field from the flag and burning it in a peaceful manner before burying the ashes, or by conducting a proper ceremony where the flag is folded in the customary triangle fold and then burned.", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 10.844, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 65.52, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
