{"id": "109", "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands lies in their exposure to the wind and resulting climate. The windward islands are exposed to the wind, specifically the northeast trade winds, making them wetter and receiving more rain. In contrast, the leeward islands are sheltered from the wind, located on the \"lee\" side, and are therefore drier, though they still receive some rain.", "raw_output": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands lies in their exposure to the wind and resulting climate. The windward islands are exposed to the wind, specifically the northeast trade winds, making them wetter and receiving more rain. In contrast, the leeward islands are sheltered from the wind, located on the \"lee\" side, and are therefore drier, though they still receive some rain.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are located in the southeastern part of the Caribbean Sea and are exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), while the Leeward Islands are located in the northwestern part of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind (\"lee\"). The main difference between them is their exposure to the wind and the resulting climate. The Windward Islands get more rain and are wetter due to their exposure to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are drier but still get rain.", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 14.625, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.16, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
