{"id": "195", "pred": "This method ensures the grouped pictures stand securely on a table top.", "raw_output": "To attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding. For joining two frames, use identical frames. For three frames, choose either three identical ones or one larger frame to serve as the middle frame.\n\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to assess the visual effect.\n\n3. Place two frames back to back and mark the hinge placement. Ensure the hinge placement is at the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to maintain stability when standing on a tabletop.\n\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\n\n5. Repeat the process for additional frames if creating a group of three.\n\nThis method ensures the grouped pictures stand securely on a table top.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo attach multiple picture frames together, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\n5. Repeat the process for additional frames, ensuring that the hinge placement is consistent across all frames.\n6. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the grouped frames and hang them up.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: Select frames with the same wood molding, lay them together, mark hinge placement, attach hinges, and attach a hanging wire to the back.", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 25.313, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.17, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "197", "pred": "Leasing is a contractual arrangement where a lessee obtains the right to use an asset owned by a lessor in exchange for periodic payments. The asset can include property, buildings, vehicles, or business equipment. The lessee pays a series of contractual, periodic, and often tax-deductible payments to the lessor for the use of the asset. This arrangement is governed by a lease agreement between the two parties, with the lessor being the legal owner and the lessee the user of the asset.", "raw_output": "Leasing is a contractual arrangement where a lessee obtains the right to use an asset owned by a lessor in exchange for periodic payments. The asset can include property, buildings, vehicles, or business equipment. The lessee pays a series of contractual, periodic, and often tax-deductible payments to the lessor for the use of the asset. This arrangement is governed by a lease agreement between the two parties, with the lessor being the legal owner and the lessee the user of the asset.", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "question": "leasing meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 17.852, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.14, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "199", "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is primarily caused by bacteria, with group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) being the most common cause. This same bacteria is responsible for conditions like strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria, such as Staphylococcus and various other pathogens, can also lead to necrotizing fasciitis, either alone or in combination with group A streptococcus. In rare cases, fungi may also cause the condition. The infection typically occurs when bacteria enter the body through minor trauma such as cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or surgical incisions, and then infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue beneath the skin.", "raw_output": "Necrotizing fasciitis is primarily caused by bacteria, with group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) being the most common cause. This same bacteria is responsible for conditions like strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria, such as Staphylococcus and various other pathogens, can also lead to necrotizing fasciitis, either alone or in combination with group A streptococcus. In rare cases, fungi may also cause the condition. The infection typically occurs when bacteria enter the body through minor trauma such as cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or surgical incisions, and then infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue beneath the skin.", "gt": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused primarily by bacteria, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci, also known as Streptococcus pyogenes. This is the same bacteria that causes strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria types, such as staphylococcus, are also associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. Prior trauma, such as a cut or scrape, insect bite, burn, or needle puncture wound can serve as a source of infection as well as surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures. In rare cases, fungi can lead to this condition.", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 27.154, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.74, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
