infection, including group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus, and trauma.", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 27.227, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "204", "pred": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot (garden beet) and other beet cultivars. It is cultivated from the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is characterized by its large, fleshy, tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be white, yellow, or red. It is similar to spinach in appearance but has a stronger, more assertive, and sometimes bitter flavor. Chard is typically cooked when mature, although young leaves can be eaten raw in salads. It is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator in plastic bags for up to 2 to 3 days.", "raw_output": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot (garden beet) and other beet cultivars. It is cultivated from the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is characterized by its large, fleshy, tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be white, yellow, or red. It is similar to spinach in appearance but has a stronger, more assertive, and sometimes bitter flavor. Chard is typically cooked when mature, although young leaves can be eaten raw in salads. It is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator in plastic bags for up to 2 to 3 days.", "gt": "Chard, also known as Swiss chard, is a vegetable with large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a flavor that is stronger and more assertive than spinach, and some people find it bitter. Chard can be eaten raw in salads when it's young, but mature leaves and stalks are usually cooked or sautéed. Chard is actually a type of beet that is grown for its leaves rather than its root. It can produce white, yellow, or red leaf stalks. Chard is highly perishable and should be kept in the refrigerator for only 2 to 3 days.", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 24.387, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.99, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
