{"id": "207", "pred": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot (garden beet) and other beet cultivars. It is cultivated from the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is characterized by its large, fleshy, tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be white, yellow, or red. It is similar to spinach in appearance but has a stronger, more assertive, and sometimes bitter flavor. Chard is typically cooked when mature, although young leaves can be eaten raw in salads. It is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator in plastic bags for up to 2 to 3 days.", "raw_output": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot (garden beet) and other beet cultivars. It is cultivated from the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is characterized by its large, fleshy, tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be white, yellow, or red. It is similar to spinach in appearance but has a stronger, more assertive, and sometimes bitter flavor. Chard is typically cooked when mature, although young leaves can be eaten raw in salads. It is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator in plastic bags for up to 2 to 3 days.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is what can be inferred about the vegetable \"chard\":\n\n* Chard is a type of beet (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) that has been chosen for leaf production over storage root formation.\n* Chard has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\n* The flavor of chard is similar to spinach but with a stronger, more assertive taste (some consider it bitter).\n* Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked to reduce bitterness and bring out a refined flavor.\n* Chard is an attractive ornamental plant that adds color to the vegetable garden.\n* Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator to minimize spoilage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is chard vegetable?\" is: A beet variety (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) grown for leaf production, characterized by large, fleshy leaves and stalks with a strong, bitter flavor that becomes more refined with cooking.", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 24.616, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.45, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "209", "pred": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot (garden beet) and other beet cultivars. It is cultivated from the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is characterized by its large, fleshy, tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be white, yellow, or red. It is similar to spinach in appearance but has a stronger, more assertive, and sometimes bitter flavor. Chard is typically cooked when mature, although young leaves can be eaten raw in salads. It is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator in plastic bags for up to 2 to 3 days.", "raw_output": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot (garden beet) and other beet cultivars. It is cultivated from the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is characterized by its large, fleshy, tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be white, yellow, or red. It is similar to spinach in appearance but has a stronger, more assertive, and sometimes bitter flavor. Chard is typically cooked when mature, although young leaves can be eaten raw in salads. It is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator in plastic bags for up to 2 to 3 days.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot and is characterized by its large, fleshy leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a stronger, more assertive flavor than spinach and can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri. Chard is a beet that has been selected for leaf production rather than storage root formation and can be harvested when young and tender or after maturity. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden, but it is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a maximum of 2-3 days.", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 24.568, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.55, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "210", "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance, composed of only one type of atom, where all atoms have the same number of protons. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together in a fixed ratio. In contrast, mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds that are not chemically bonded and retain their individual identities. Mixtures have variable composition, and their components can be separated by physical methods. Unlike compounds, mixtures do not form new substances, and they exhibit the properties of their constituent substances.", "raw_output": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance, composed of only one type of atom, where all atoms have the same number of protons. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together in a fixed ratio. In contrast, mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds that are not chemically bonded and retain their individual identities. Mixtures have variable composition, and their components can be separated by physical methods. Unlike compounds, mixtures do not form new substances, and they exhibit the properties of their constituent substances.", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, meaning all the atoms in an element have the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other. Mixtures have variable compositions and show the properties of their constituent substances. Elements and compounds just mix together to form a mixture and no new compound is formed.", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 19.549, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 71.83, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
