n the lift arm.", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 38.862, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.05, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "227", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, remove the old flapper and chain, install the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, secure it with pliers, connect the lift arm to the flush handle, and adjust the chain as needed after flushing to ensure proper operation.", "raw_output": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm (closest to the edge).\n5. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, tighten it securely.\n7. Turn the water valve back on to fill the tank.\n8. Flush the toilet to test operation.\n9. If needed, adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a few links to ensure proper function.\n10. Once satisfied, cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n\nAnswer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, remove the old flapper and chain, install the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, secure it with pliers, connect the lift arm to the flush handle, and adjust the chain as needed after flushing to ensure proper operation.", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here's a brief answer on how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on the given passages:\n\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain for a 1.6 gallon per flush toilet.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 38.955, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.32, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "231", "pred": "Oil stains on concrete driveways are common and can be challenging to remove. The effectiveness of removal depends on the size of the spill and how long the stain has been present. Several methods can be used to clean oil stains, including applying a commercial-grade cleaner and scrubbing with a brush or broom, followed by using a pressure washer with detergent. It is important to avoid using a high-pressure hose, as it may push the oil deeper into the concrete. Alternative methods include using oven cleaner, Goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner, as demonstrated in a comparison video. For fresh or stubborn stains, the poultice method may also be effective.", "raw_output": "Oil stains on concrete driveways are common and can be challenging to remove. The effectiveness of removal depends on the size of the spill and how long the stain has been present. Several methods can be used to clean oil stains, including applying a commercial-grade cleaner and scrubbing with a brush or broom, followed by using a pressure washer with detergent. It is important to avoid using a high-pressure hose, as it may push the oil deeper into the concrete. Alternative methods include using oven cleaner, Goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner, as demonstrated in a comparison video. For fresh or stubborn stains, the poultice method may also be effective.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 22.713, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.64, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "233", "pred": "Sausalito has a mild climate with an average yearly temperature range from a low of 43°F in January to a high of 69°F in July. The city receives 34 inches of rain annually, with the most precipitation occurring in January. There is no snowfall, and the city enjoys an average of 256 sunny days per year. The monthly average temperature in September reaches up to 58°F, while December's average temperature is 50°F. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable climate year-round, which is significantly better than the national average of 54.", "raw_output": "Sausalito has a mild climate with an average yearly temperature range from a low of 43°F in January to a high of 69°F in July. The city receives 34 inches of rain annually, with the most precipitation occurring in January. There is no snowfall, and the city enjoys an average of 256 sunny days per year. The monthly average temperature in September reaches up to 58°F, while December's average temperature is 50°F. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable climate year-round, which is significantly better than the national average of 54.", "gt": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "question": "average weather sausalito", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 23.317, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "235", "pred": "Sausalito has a mild climate with an average yearly temperature range from a low of 43°F in January to a high of 69°F in July. The city receives 34 inches of rain annually, with the most precipitation occurring in January. There is no snowfall, and the city enjoys an average of 256 sunny days per year. The monthly average temperature in September reaches up to 58°F, while December's average temperature is 50°F. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable climate year-round, which is significantly better than the national average of 54.", "raw_output": "Sausalito has a mild climate with an average yearly temperature range from a low of 43°F in January to a high of 69°F in July. The city receives 34 inches of rain annually, with the most precipitation occurring in January. There is no snowfall, and the city enjoys an average of 256 sunny days per year. The monthly average temperature in September reaches up to 58°F, while December's average temperature is 50°F. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable climate year-round, which is significantly better than the national average of 54.", "gt": "Average weather in Sausalito can vary depending on the time of year. For example, during September, the average temperature is 58 degrees Fahrenheit (15 degrees Celsius), while in January, it is only 43 degrees Fahrenheit (4 degrees Celsius). The most precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches. However, throughout the year, the number of days with measurable precipitation is 56, and there are an average of 256 sunny days.", "question": "average weather sausalito", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 23.311, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.57, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "236", "pred": "Sausalito has a mild climate with an average yearly temperature range from a low of 43°F in January to a high of 69°F in July. The city receives 34 inches of rain annually, with the most precipitation occurring in January. There is no snowfall, and the city enjoys an average of 256 sunny days per year. The monthly average temperature in September reaches up to 58°F, while December's average temperature is 50°F. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable climate year-round, which is significantly better than the national average of 54.", "raw_output": "Sausalito has a mild climate with an average yearly temperature range from a low of 43°F in January to a high of 69°F in July. The city receives 34 inches of rain annually, with the most precipitation occurring in January. There is no snowfall, and the city enjoys an average of 256 sunny days per year. The monthly average temperature in September reaches up to 58°F, while December's average temperature is 50°F. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable climate year-round, which is significantly better than the national average of 54.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "question": "average weather sausalito", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 23.386, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.74, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "240", "pred": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit but preventing them from exiting. They are typically large, square-shaped structures made of wire or metal mesh, reinforced with steel bars. Two sides of the trap have angled lead-ins that guide crabs toward the entrance. Once inside, the crabs are unable to escape due to the design of the trap. The traps are baited to attract crabs, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the food, which leads them into the trap.", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit but preventing them from exiting. They are typically large, square-shaped structures made of wire or metal mesh, reinforced with steel bars. Two sides of the trap have angled lead-ins that guide crabs toward the entrance. Once inside, the crabs are unable to escape due to the design of the trap. The traps are baited to attract crabs, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the food, which leads them into the trap.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a crab trap is a large square metal cage with a system of nets inside that allows crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the top. To set the trap, the ends with lead-ins are placed in the water and the crabs are attracted to the free meal offered by the trap. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game recommends using king crab pots that range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights between 2 and 3 feet. Over time, these mechanisms may disable the trap, preventing it from ghost fishing.", "question": "how do crab traps work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 18.691, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.21, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "242", "pred": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit but preventing them from exiting. They are typically large, square-shaped structures made of wire or metal mesh, reinforced with steel bars. Two sides of the trap have angled lead-ins that guide crabs toward the entrance. Once inside, the crabs are unable to escape due to the design of the trap. The traps are baited to attract crabs, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the food, which leads them into the trap.", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit but preventing them from exiting. They are typically large, square-shaped structures made of wire or metal mesh, reinforced with steel bars. Two sides of the trap have angled lead-ins that guide crabs toward the entrance. Once inside, the crabs are unable to escape due to the design of the trap. The traps are baited to attract crabs, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the food, which leads them into the trap.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are made of a metal cage with a system of nets inside, which are designed to allow crabs to enter but not escape. The traps have two leads that angle into the pot from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit entrance. The crabs crawl up the leads to reach the bait inside the pot, but cannot exit through the slit. The pot is designed to keep the crabs inside until they can be retrieved by the fisherman.\n\nAdditionally, according to passage 3, crab pots can be equipped with mechanisms that disable them over time, preventing them from continuing to catch crabs after they have been abandoned or become lost. These mechanisms can include biodegradable mesh or dissolvable cords.", "question": "how do crab traps work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 18.746, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.61, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "243", "pred": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit but preventing them from exiting. They are typically large, square-shaped structures made of wire or metal mesh, reinforced with steel bars. Two sides of the trap have angled lead-ins that guide crabs toward the entrance. Once inside, the crabs are unable to escape due to the design of the trap. The traps are baited to attract crabs, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the food, which leads them into the trap.", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit but preventing them from exiting. They are typically large, square-shaped structures made of wire or metal mesh, reinforced with steel bars. Two sides of the trap have angled lead-ins that guide crabs toward the entrance. Once inside, the crabs are unable to escape due to the design of the trap. The traps are baited to attract crabs, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the food, which leads them into the trap.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are large square structures made of wire or flat metal mesh, with two ends that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. Crabs are attracted to bait inside the pot and must crawl up the leads to reach it, but once they enter, they cannot escape due to the narrow opening. The pot is designed to allow crabs in but not let them out, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How do crab traps work?\" is: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage with a narrow entrance that allows crabs to enter but not exit, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.", "question": "how do crab traps work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 