{"id": "252", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.\n2. Rinse the pork chops.\n3. Prepare a spice mixture by combining seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring.\n4. Sprinkle the spice mixture on both sides of the wet pork chops.\n5. Use your hands to massage the spice rub into the meat.\n6. Let the seasoned pork chops stand for 10 minutes.\n7. Grill the chops over indirect heat until they are no longer pink inside, approximately 12 minutes per side.", "raw_output": "To grill pork chops according to the provided passage:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.\n2. Rinse the pork chops.\n3. Prepare a spice mixture by combining seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring.\n4. Sprinkle the spice mixture on both sides of the wet pork chops.\n5. Use your hands to massage the spice rub into the meat.\n6. Let the seasoned pork chops stand for 10 minutes.\n7. Grill the chops over indirect heat until they are no longer pink inside, approximately 12 minutes per side.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. (Passage 1)\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. (Passage 1)\n3. For Oven-Fried Pork Chops, use stuffing mix for the breading. The pork chops come out tender and juicy. This recipe takes 30 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to prep. (Passage 2)\n4. To grill pork chops over indirect heat, rinse the chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat for 10 minutes before grilling. Grill the chops until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com, you should preheat the grill, season the pork chops with a spice mixture, and grill them over indirect heat until they are cooked through.", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 22.956, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.29, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "255", "pred": "Regular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "raw_output": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct is not fastened or sealed, it should slide right out.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to clean lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n\nAdditionally, for a more thorough cleaning:\n- Remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean that area.\n- Pay attention to the area around the lint filter.\n- Remove the lint filter frame to gain better access to lint deposits and use a vacuum nozzle for deeper cleaning.\n\nRegular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "gt": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove the cover.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole of the vent.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n6. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning that area as well.\n7. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access to clean.\n8. This thorough cleaning will help your dryer run efficiently and reduce the risk of house fires.\n\nNote: The information provided in the given passages is sufficient to answer the question.", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 31.965, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.54, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "256", "pred": "Regular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "raw_output": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct is not fastened or sealed, it should slide right out.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to clean lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n\nAdditionally, for a more thorough cleaning:\n- Remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean that area.\n- Pay attention to the area around the lint filter.\n- Remove the lint filter frame to gain better access to lint deposits and use a vacuum nozzle for deeper cleaning.\n\nRegular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "gt": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 31.792, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.57, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "257", "pred": "Regular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "raw_output": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct is not fastened or sealed, it should slide right out.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to clean lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n\nAdditionally, for a more thorough cleaning:\n- Remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean that area.\n- Pay attention to the area around the lint filter.\n- Remove the lint filter frame to gain better access to lint deposits and use a vacuum nozzle for deeper cleaning.\n\nRegular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the steps to clean a dryer vent based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house (passage 1) and remove it by sliding it out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the exterior (step 2).\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the hole where the vent connects to the dryer (step 3).\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint (step 4).\n4. Clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (step 4).\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (step 5).\n6. If desired, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter (passage 2).\n7. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits in the area around the lint filter frame (passage 2).\n\nNote: Passage 3 provides additional information but does not provide specific instructions for cleaning the dryer vent. Therefore, these steps are based on the information provided in passages 1-2.", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 31.778, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.76, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "259", "pred": "Regular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "raw_output": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct is not fastened or sealed, it should slide right out.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to clean lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n\nAdditionally, for a more thorough cleaning:\n- Remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean that area.\n- Pay attention to the area around the lint filter.\n- Remove the lint filter frame to gain better access to lint deposits and use a vacuum nozzle for deeper cleaning.\n\nRegular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean dryer vent\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo clean the dryer vent, start by locating the vent cover on the outside of the house and removing it. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer and use a dryer vent brush to clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning the area around the lint filter for a more thorough cleaning. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits and ensure your dryer runs efficiently.\n\nIf the passages did not contain the necessary information to answer the question, I would have replied with \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 31.967, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.12, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "260", "pred": "1. Improving oxygen efficiency in the blood with the same amount of work.\n2. Increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable.\n3. Enhancing nutrient absorption, including vitamins and minerals.\n4. Supporting the full utilization of Co-enzyme Q10, which requires sulfur (MSM) to be effective.\n5. Relieving muscular aches and pains.\n6. Reducing inflammation caused by injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis by helping regulate cellular water pressure and swelling.", "raw_output": "The benefits of MSM powder include:\n\n1. Improving oxygen efficiency in the blood with the same amount of work.\n2. Increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable.\n3. Enhancing nutrient absorption, including vitamins and minerals.\n4. Supporting the full utilization of Co-enzyme Q10, which requires sulfur (MSM) to be effective.\n5. Relieving muscular aches and pains.\n6. Reducing inflammation caused by injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis by helping regulate cellular water pressure and swelling.", "gt": "MSM powder offers several benefits. It helps get oxygen into the blood more efficiently, thereby increasing energy levels. It also makes cell walls more permeable. The powder aids in the absorption of more nutrients, particularly when paired with Co-enzyme Q10. Additionally, MSM powder can help relieve muscular aches and pains and reduce inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "question": "the benefits of msm powder", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 18.317, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.18, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
