{"id": "304", "pred": "Watermelons explode due to the buildup of gas inside them as they rot. This gas increases the internal pressure, and when the pressure becomes too great for the watermelon's skin to contain, it causes the watermelon to explode.", "raw_output": "Watermelons explode due to the buildup of gas inside them as they rot. This gas increases the internal pressure, and when the pressure becomes too great for the watermelon's skin to contain, it causes the watermelon to explode.", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 9.219, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.25, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "310", "pred": "The average cost to install a second floor in a house ranges from $100 to $300 per square foot for a typical addition (such as 2-3 bedrooms, a bath, and a flight of stairs). However, depending on the complexity, quality of materials, and local labor rates, the cost can increase to $400-$500 per square foot. Additionally, building a second floor typically costs at least 20 percent more than constructing the same square footage at ground level.", "raw_output": "The average cost to install a second floor in a house ranges from $100 to $300 per square foot for a typical addition (such as 2-3 bedrooms, a bath, and a flight of stairs). However, depending on the complexity, quality of materials, and local labor rates, the cost can increase to $400-$500 per square foot. Additionally, building a second floor typically costs at least 20 percent more than constructing the same square footage at ground level.", "gt": "Hiring a remodeling contractor to build a second floor addition can cost between $100-$300 a square foot for a typical addition, but the cost can go as high as $400-$500 per square foot depending on the complexity, quality of materials and local labor rates. Building a second floor can cost at least 20 percent more than building the same square footage at ground level.", "question": "avg cost to install a second floor in a house", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 18.661, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
