{"id": "403", "pred": "The provided passages do not contain specific instructions for removing the door panel on a 2006 Chevy Impala. While passage 2 mentions that a video applies to the Chevy Impala model years 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11, and 12, it does not provide detailed steps for removing the door panel. Therefore, based on the information given, it is not possible to provide specific removal instructions for the 2006 Chevy door panel.", "raw_output": "Answer: The provided passages do not contain specific instructions for removing the door panel on a 2006 Chevy Impala. While passage 2 mentions that a video applies to the Chevy Impala model years 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11, and 12, it does not provide detailed steps for removing the door panel. Therefore, based on the information given, it is not possible to provide specific removal instructions for the 2006 Chevy door panel.", "gt": "To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle. You will also need to remove a pin on the outer edge of the door. Once these are removed, you can use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 19.642, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.18, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
