{"id": "428", "pred": "Twins happen when two offspring are produced by the same pregnancy. They can be of two types: monozygotic (identical) or dizygotic (fraternal). Monozygotic twins occur when a single zygote splits into two embryos, typically within the first 8 days after fertilization. Dizygotic twins occur when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, resulting in two distinct embryos.", "raw_output": "Twins happen when two offspring are produced by the same pregnancy. They can be of two types: monozygotic (identical) or dizygotic (fraternal). Monozygotic twins occur when a single zygote splits into two embryos, typically within the first 8 days after fertilization. Dizygotic twins occur when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, resulting in two distinct embryos.", "gt": "Twins are two offspring produced by the same pregnancy. They can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning they develop from one zygote that splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning they develop from two different eggs with each being fertilized by its own sperm cell. Monoamniotic twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization. Dizygotic twin pregnancies are more likely in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, aged between 30 and 40 years, of above average height and weight, and who have had several previous pregnancies.", "question": "how do twins happen", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 16.011, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.06, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "429", "pred": "Twins happen when two offspring are produced by the same pregnancy. They can be of two types: monozygotic (identical) or dizygotic (fraternal). Monozygotic twins occur when a single zygote splits into two embryos, typically within the first 8 days after fertilization. Dizygotic twins occur when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, resulting in two distinct embryos.", "raw_output": "Twins happen when two offspring are produced by the same pregnancy. They can be of two types: monozygotic (identical) or dizygotic (fraternal). Monozygotic twins occur when a single zygote splits into two embryos, typically within the first 8 days after fertilization. Dizygotic twins occur when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, resulting in two distinct embryos.", "gt": "Twins can happen in two ways: monozygotic (identical) twins occur when one zygote splits into two embryos, while dizygotic (fraternal) twins happen when two different eggs are fertilized by two separate sperm cells. The likelihood of dizygotic twins is influenced by factors such as West African descent, being between 30 and 40 years old, being taller and heavier than average, and having had several previous pregnancies. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the zygote happens within 8 days of fertilization and can result in complications due to shared organs.", "question": "how do twins happen", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 16.135, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.46, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "430", "pred": "Twins happen when two offspring are produced by the same pregnancy. They can be of two types: monozygotic (identical) or dizygotic (fraternal). Monozygotic twins occur when a single zygote splits into two embryos, typically within the first 8 days after fertilization. Dizygotic twins occur when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, resulting in two distinct embryos.", "raw_output": "Twins happen when two offspring are produced by the same pregnancy. They can be of two types: monozygotic (identical) or dizygotic (fraternal). Monozygotic twins occur when a single zygote splits into two embryos, typically within the first 8 days after fertilization. Dizygotic twins occur when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, resulting in two distinct embryos.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how twins happen:\n\n* Monoamniotic twins: These twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization.\n* Conjoined twins: When the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs, it happens within 8 days of fertilization, and mortality is highest for conjoined twins due to the many complications resulting from shared organs.\n* Dizygotic twin pregnancies: These twins are slightly more likely to occur in women who are of West African descent (especially Yoruba), between the ages of 30 and 40, are taller and heavier than average, and have had several previous pregnancies.\n* Identical twins (monozygotic): These twins develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos.\n* Fraternal twins (dizygotic): These twins develop from two different eggs, and each twin is fertilized by its own sperm cell.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages: The passage does not provide information on the exact timing or mechanism of twinning beyond what is mentioned above.", "question": "how do twins happen", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 16.039, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.71, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "431", "pred": "These methods are effective for cleaning tarnished jewelry at home without damaging the pieces", "raw_output": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use several methods depending on the type of jewelry and the severity of tarnish:\n\n1. For silver jewelry that is dull, filmy, or starting to discolor: Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water. Dip a soft cloth into the solution, rub the jewelry, rinse with cool water, and buff dry with a cloth.\n\n2. For heavier tarnish on silver: Create a paste using three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the paste with a soft, lint-free cloth (avoid paper towels, as they can scratch).\n\n3. For a gentle cleaning method that removes tarnish without abrasion: Use a saltwater bath. Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl (enough to cover the jewelry). This method works well for lightly tarnished silver. If cleaning multiple pieces, use more water; for a single piece, use less. However, if the jewelry has gemstones, ensure they are not affected by submersion in saltwater.\n\n4. For diamond jewelry: Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat dry with a soft cloth.\n\nThese methods are effective for cleaning tarnished jewelry at home without damaging the pieces", "gt": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first determine the extent of the tarnish. If the jewelry is slightly dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth into the solution. Rub the jewelry with the cloth, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. If the tarnish is heavier, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the jewelry and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. If your silver jewelry is lightly tarnished, you can also try submerging it in a hot saltwater bath. Ensure that if your jewelry has gemstones, they won't be affected by the saltwater. For diamonds, clean with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, and pat dry with a soft cloth.", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 41.953, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
