{"id": "434", "pred": "These methods are effective for cleaning tarnished jewelry at home without damaging the pieces", "raw_output": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use several methods depending on the type of jewelry and the severity of tarnish:\n\n1. For silver jewelry that is dull, filmy, or starting to discolor: Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water. Dip a soft cloth into the solution, rub the jewelry, rinse with cool water, and buff dry with a cloth.\n\n2. For heavier tarnish on silver: Create a paste using three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the paste with a soft, lint-free cloth (avoid paper towels, as they can scratch).\n\n3. For a gentle cleaning method that removes tarnish without abrasion: Use a saltwater bath. Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl (enough to cover the jewelry). This method works well for lightly tarnished silver. If cleaning multiple pieces, use more water; for a single piece, use less. However, if the jewelry has gemstones, ensure they are not affected by submersion in saltwater.\n\n4. For diamond jewelry: Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat dry with a soft cloth.\n\nThese methods are effective for cleaning tarnished jewelry at home without damaging the pieces", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean tarnished jewelry at home\":\n\nTo clean tarnished jewelry at home, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth in the solution. Rub the jewelry gently, then rinse it in cool water and buff it with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water and apply it with a soft, lint-free cloth. You can also use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl and submerging the jewelry in it. Let it sit for a while, then remove and rinse it with cool water. Be sure to use a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds.", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 41.981, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.52, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "435", "pred": "Additionally, if you", "raw_output": "To find someone in France, you can use the following methods:\n\n1. Use a people search website for France, which may help locate individuals, especially if you know their city of birth. You can contact the town hall in the city where the person was born by sending an email or letter.\n\n2. Try the French white pages in English at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. Instead of entering \"Paris\" in the City field, enter \"IDF\" (or \"Ile de France\") in the Dept district or region field to search Paris and its suburbs.\n\n3. Visit www.pagesjaunes.fr (the Pages Blanches, the French version of the white pages). Enter the person's last name in the \"Nom\" field and optionally their first name in the \"Prenom\" field. If you have address information, enter it in the \"Ou\" section; otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. Click \"Trouver\" to search for the name. The results will display the name, address, and phone number for all matching listings.\n\n4. Post a \"missed connection\" (MC) on Paris Craigslist at http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers.\n\nAdditionally, if you", "gt": "To find someone in France, you can use a website for people search in France. Sending an email or letter to the Town Hall in the person's city of birth can also be helpful, especially if you have lost relatives or friends. Try to find out the person's middle name, it could make the search easier. You can also use the French white pages, available in English at www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the 'Nom' field and first name in the 'Prenom' field, enter address information if known, and then click 'Trouver' to search. For searching in Paris and its suburbs, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. Posting a missed connection on Paris Craigslist might also be helpful.", "question": "how to find someone in france", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 42.224, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.13, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
