{"id": "471", "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil (also called pure or virgin coconut oil) is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil has a mild coconut flavor and aroma. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450°F compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350°F, making refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "raw_output": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil (also called pure or virgin coconut oil) is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil has a mild coconut flavor and aroma. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450°F compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350°F, making refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "gt": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, has no discernible taste or smell, and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 23.581, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.54, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
