{"id": "539", "pred": "The song is credited to Bob Dylan as the songwriter.", "raw_output": "The lyrics \"He was a friend of mine\" are repeated throughout the song, with variations in the verses. Some of the lyrics include:\n\n- \"He was a friend of mine, he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny, he didn't have a dime, he was a friend of mine.\"\n- \"He died neath the midnight sun, he died neath the midnight sun.\"\n- \"And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine.\"\n- \"Every time I hear his name, Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\"\n\nThe song is credited to Bob Dylan as the songwriter.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are mentioned in the following passages:\n\n* Passage 1: In the context of the Greenbriar Boys recording the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" with singer Dian James in 1963.\n* Passage 2: As part of a fragmented repetition of the line \"He was a friend of mine\" in the passage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nPassage 1 and Passage 2", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 28.992, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.35, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
