{"id": "620", "pred": "Technology has changed the workplace in several significant ways. It has increased efficiency and productivity, transformed business operations, and altered workplace dynamics. Over the past 10 to 15 years, rapid technological advancements have reshaped the office environment, making it more flexible and global. Employees can now interact with a global market and work remotely, moving away from the traditional office setup of the past.", "raw_output": "Technology has changed the workplace in several significant ways. It has increased efficiency and productivity, transformed business operations, and altered workplace dynamics. Over the past 10 to 15 years, rapid technological advancements have reshaped the office environment, making it more flexible and global. Employees can now interact with a global market and work remotely, moving away from the traditional office setup of the past.", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 14.13, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.4, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
