"has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 13.971, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.72, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "627", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "raw_output": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "gt": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay close to them when they are near the three-point line, actively sliding your feet to minimize shot opportunities (passage 1). It is important to create a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player (passage 3).", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 10.462, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.86, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "628", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "raw_output": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "gt": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you can stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, you can keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player and defend against them with tips from an experienced basketball player.", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 10.354, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.23, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "629", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "raw_output": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some strategies for guarding a tall person in basketball:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard them near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities (Passage 1).\n2. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, to guard a tall person in basketball, it is important to stay close to them and create a barrier between them and the basket. These strategies can help limit their shooting opportunities and make it more difficult for them to score.", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 10.535, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.56, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "630", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "raw_output": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to guard a tall person in basketball:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall, skilled shooter when guarding them near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player.\n\nTherefore, to guard a tall person in basketball, it is essential to stay close to them, move quickly laterally to maintain position, and use a defensive strategy such as keeping a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 10.452, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.33, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "631", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "raw_output": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them, especially near the three-point line, and actively slide your feet side to side to maintain position and limit their shot opportunities. Additionally, maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against them.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to guard a tall person in basketball\":\n\nTo guard a tall person in basketball, it's important to stay as close as possible to them when they're near the three-point line. Slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against them effectively.", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 10.446, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.53, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "632", "pred": "The nervous system and endocrine system both maintain homeostasis and use chemical messengers regulated by negative feedback. However, the nervous system uses interconnected neurons and electrochemical signals, while the endocrine system uses glands and hormones transmitted via the circulatory system.", "raw_output": "Similarities:\n- Both the nervous system and the endocrine system are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n- Both systems use chemical messengers (neurotransmitters in the nervous system and hormones in the endocrine system).\n- Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n\nDifferences:\n- The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n- The nervous system transmits signals via electrochemical pulses, whereas the endocrine system uses hormones for signal transmission.\n- The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, while the endocrine system consists of discrete, non-physically connected organs.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system to distribute hormones.\n\nAnswer: The nervous system and endocrine system both maintain homeostasis and use chemical messengers regulated by negative feedback. However, the nervous system uses interconnected neurons and electrochemical signals, while the endocrine system uses glands and hormones transmitted via the circulatory system.", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system are both critical to maintaining homeostasis in the body by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. They both use chemical messengers, although their method of transmission and release differs. The nervous system is made of interconnected neuron cells and uses electrochemical pulses for signal transmission. In contrast, the endocrine system is made of discrete glands that use hormones for signal transmission and utilizes the circulatory system to carry these signals.", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 36.286, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.38, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "633", "pred": "The nervous system and endocrine system both maintain homeostasis and use chemical messengers regulated by negative feedback. However, the nervous system uses interconnected neurons and electrochemical signals, while the endocrine system uses glands and hormones transmitted via the circulatory system.", "raw_output": "Similarities:\n- Both the nervous system and the endocrine system are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n- Both systems use chemical messengers (neurotransmitters in the nervous system and hormones in the endocrine system).\n- Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n\nDifferences:\n- The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n- The nervous system transmits signals via electrochemical pulses, whereas the endocrine system uses hormones for signal transmission.\n- The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, while the endocrine system consists of discrete, non-physically connected organs.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system to distribute hormones.\n\nAnswer: The nervous system and endocrine system both maintain homeostasis and use chemical messengers regulated by negative feedback. However, the nervous system uses interconnected neurons and electrochemical signals, while the endocrine system uses glands and hormones transmitted via the circulatory system.", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system have both similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n1. Both systems are dedicated to maintaining homeostasis and coordinating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers play a crucial role in both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while chemical hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system utilizes interconnected cells to transmit signals, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 36.301, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.66, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
