s:\n- The nervous system is made up of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses while transmission in the endocrine system is done through chemicals called hormones.\n- The nervous system is a continuous network of interconnected cells while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs that are not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 36.205, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.34, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
