{"id": "695", "pred": "To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "raw_output": "To make ice cream, you can follow these general steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Prepare the ice cream base. For a cream-based ice cream, mix sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Stir in vanilla extract, then chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\n\n2. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, typically for 20 to 25 minutes, until the ice cream is softly frozen.\n\n3. Serve immediately for a soft-serve texture, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the surface of the ice cream and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to allow it to ripen and firm up.\n\nAlternatively, you can use a cold ice cream mix directly in the ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes, then serve or freeze as desired.\n\nAnswer: To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "gt": "To make ice cream, you start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Next, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 41.572, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.84, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "696", "pred": "To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "raw_output": "To make ice cream, you can follow these general steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Prepare the ice cream base. For a cream-based ice cream, mix sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Stir in vanilla extract, then chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\n\n2. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, typically for 20 to 25 minutes, until the ice cream is softly frozen.\n\n3. Serve immediately for a soft-serve texture, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the surface of the ice cream and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to allow it to ripen and firm up.\n\nAlternatively, you can use a cold ice cream mix directly in the ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes, then serve or freeze as desired.\n\nAnswer: To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "gt": "To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 41.744, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.78, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "697", "pred": "To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "raw_output": "To make ice cream, you can follow these general steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Prepare the ice cream base. For a cream-based ice cream, mix sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Stir in vanilla extract, then chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\n\n2. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, typically for 20 to 25 minutes, until the ice cream is softly frozen.\n\n3. Serve immediately for a soft-serve texture, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the surface of the ice cream and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to allow it to ripen and firm up.\n\nAlternatively, you can use a cold ice cream mix directly in the ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes, then serve or freeze as desired.\n\nAnswer: To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "gt": "To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to manufacturer's instructions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. For a creamy and flavorful base, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly before using it as a base for your desired ice cream flavor.", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 41.679, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.74, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "698", "pred": "To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "raw_output": "To make ice cream, you can follow these general steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Prepare the ice cream base. For a cream-based ice cream, mix sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Stir in vanilla extract, then chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\n\n2. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, typically for 20 to 25 minutes, until the ice cream is softly frozen.\n\n3. Serve immediately for a soft-serve texture, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the surface of the ice cream and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to allow it to ripen and firm up.\n\nAlternatively, you can use a cold ice cream mix directly in the ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes, then serve or freeze as desired.\n\nAnswer: To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\nPassage 1 provides instructions for making ice cream using an ice cream maker. To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes). Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nPassage 2 provides a recipe for making ice cream from scratch. To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Then, heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n\nPassage 3 provides general instructions for making ice cream bases. To make ice cream, you will need to start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This type of base is made with cream rather than custard, and it results in a lighter and less icy texture. To make one quart of ice cream, you will need to double the recipe.\n\nTherefore, to summarize:\n\nTo make ice cream using an ice cream maker:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and turn on the machine.\n2. Churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes).\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nTo make ice cream from scratch:\n\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges.\n3. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract.\n4. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 41.585, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.81, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "699", "pred": "To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "raw_output": "To make ice cream, you can follow these general steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Prepare the ice cream base. For a cream-based ice cream, mix sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Stir in vanilla extract, then chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\n\n2. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, typically for 20 to 25 minutes, until the ice cream is softly frozen.\n\n3. Serve immediately for a soft-serve texture, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the surface of the ice cream and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to allow it to ripen and firm up.\n\nAlternatively, you can use a cold ice cream mix directly in the ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes, then serve or freeze as desired.\n\nAnswer: To make ice cream, prepare a base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves, then chill it. Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. Serve immediately", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved, then heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2).\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2).\n4. Once the ice cream base is ready, pour it into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\n\nNote that the passages do not provide a specific recipe for making ice cream, but rather provide general steps and tips for making ice cream using an ice cream maker.", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 41.851, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.66, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "701", "pred": "Children learn several things through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water. In terms of academic learning, they explore science concepts such as floating and sinking, and in math, they learn about measuring, comparing quantities like \"more\" and \"less,\" and understanding volume. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children engage in pretend play.", "raw_output": "Children learn several things through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water. In terms of academic learning, they explore science concepts such as floating and sinking, and in math, they learn about measuring, comparing quantities like \"more\" and \"less,\" and understanding volume. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children engage in pretend play.", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. It aids in the development of gross motor skills as they engage in activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water from buckets. Water play also facilitates academic learning in areas such as science and math. Children learn about the concept of floating and sinking, and understand that different objects have different buoyancies. In math, they learn about measurement by determining the amount of water that fits into a bucket, and concepts of more and less by comparing water levels in different buckets. Water play also promotes creativity, allowing children to use their imagination.", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 14.092, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.41, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "702", "pred": "Children learn several things through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water. In terms of academic learning, they explore science concepts such as floating and sinking, and in math, they learn about measuring, comparing quantities like \"more\" and \"less,\" and understanding volume. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children engage in pretend play.", "raw_output": "Children learn several things through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water. In terms of academic learning, they explore science concepts such as floating and sinking, and in math, they learn about measuring, comparing quantities like \"more\" and \"less,\" and understanding volume. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children engage in pretend play.", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers and pouring water. Water play also provides opportunities for academic learning, such as understanding concepts like floating and sinking, measuring water, and comparing quantities. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children pretend and engage in imaginative play with water.", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 14.14, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 73.33, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "705", "pred": "Children learn several things through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water. In terms of academic learning, they explore science concepts such as floating and sinking, and in math, they learn about measuring, comparing quantities like \"more\" and \"less,\" and understanding volume. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children engage in pretend play.", "raw_output": "Children learn several things through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water. In terms of academic learning, they explore science concepts such as floating and sinking, and in math, they learn about measuring, comparing quantities like \"more\" and \"less,\" and understanding volume. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children engage in pretend play.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 14.213, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.7, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "706", "pred": "The colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n- White symbolizes purity.\n- Blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee.\n- Red represents the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\n\nThese colors are also the national colors of the United States.", "raw_output": "The colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n- White symbolizes purity.\n- Blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee.\n- Red represents the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\n\nThese colors are also the national colors of the United States.", "gt": "The colors on the Tennessee Flag have significant meanings. The white color symbolizes purity, the blue color stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and the red color represents the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. The three white stars within the blue circle symbolize the three disparate forms of land that divide the state.", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 10.876, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.5, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
