-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "717", "pred": "The PoachPod® is a flexible silicone tool designed to help poach eggs with ease, and it can also be used for baking and molding. It is dishwasher safe for easy cleanup.", "raw_output": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod (as mentioned in the instructions).\n3. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n4. Carefully float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod.\n5. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for approximately 4–6 minutes (some instructions suggest 6 minutes).\n6. Remove the lid and use a slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the water.\n7. Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly poached egg.\n\nThe PoachPod® is a flexible silicone tool designed to help poach eggs with ease, and it can also be used for baking and molding. It is dishwasher safe for easy cleanup.", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, first, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod, then crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it remains upright and no water gets inside. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for about six minutes. After cooking, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Finally, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate. The PoachPod can be cleaned in a dishwasher.", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "vcd", "has_vcd": false, "time_sec": 34.832, "status": "success", "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.53, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
